\description{
\code{cv.bregsurv()} is the main function of the package. It fits a model to your data while borrowing
from what an external source made available, by minimizing
\deqn{Q_\eta(\theta) = -\ell(\theta) + \eta\, B_G(\theta), \qquad \eta \ge 0,}
the negative log-likelihood \eqn{\ell} of your data plus an integration weight \eqn{\eta} times a
Bregman divergence \eqn{B_G} between your model and the external one. \eqn{\eta = 0} ignores the
external source and larger values borrow more; \code{cv.bregsurv()} chooses \eqn{\eta} (and, under a
penalty, the penalty level) by cross-validation on your data.

A call is made of four choices, one per argument:
\enumerate{
\item \code{target}: the model you fit to your own data, which fixes \eqn{\ell};
\item \code{release}: what the external source made available;
\item \code{divergence}: how the release enters the objective, which fixes \eqn{B_G};
\item \code{penalty}: an optional ridge, lasso or elastic-net penalty on the coefficients.
}
}
